/*
 * Job Radar relevance fixtures: real Greenhouse job details (captured 2026-11-21, company names replaced). Two were
 * reported as wrong matches for "Data Architect / Senior Data Engineer"; the third is a genuine data engineering job.
 */
(function () {
  globalThis.RADAR_FIXTURES = Object.assign(globalThis.RADAR_FIXTURES || {}, { relevance: {"dataCenter": {"id": 5468374008, "title": "Data Center Power Generation and Microgrids Engineer", "location": {"name": "Remote-Friendly, United States"}, "content": "&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Initech&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Initech’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Training and serving frontier AI models requires compute infrastructure at a scale and density that pushes past what conventional data center designs were built to handle. The loads involved are large enough — and arrive fast enough — that utility supply alone often can&#39;t meet the need on the timeline required, and the step-load behavior of large accelerator clusters creates power-quality and ride-through demands that conventional backup-generation designs weren&#39;t built for. Initech&#39;s Data Center Infrastructure team is responsible for solving that problem: delivering facilities that can be energized early, ride through grid disturbances, and present a well-behaved load at the point of interconnection (POI).&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;As a Data Center Power Generation &amp;amp; Microgrids Engineer, you&#39;ll own the behind-the-meter generation and storage architecture for Initech&#39;s data center portfolio. That means the on-site generation fleet — reciprocating engine gensets, gas turbines, fuel cells — and the battery energy storage systems that buffer load steps and provide ride-through. It means the microgrid layer that ties them together: islanding and resynchronization, black-start, load-shedding, and generation dispatch. And it means the grid side: interconnection studies and agreements, IEEE 1547/2800 compliance, and power quality at the point of interconnection. You&#39;ll also own our temporary- and bridging-generation strategies — the plans that let a site energize and start serving load before permanent utility service is available, and transition cleanly once it is.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This is a deeply cross-functional role. You&#39;ll work closely with colleagues across the infrastructure team on where and how generation and storage tie into the site electrical distribution, controls, and SCADA, and with our hardware and compute teams to understand the load characteristics you&#39;re designing against. You&#39;ll be Initech&#39;s technical counterpart to on-site generation providers, BESS integrators, utilities, and ISOs/RTOs. Expect roughly 20–35% travel for design reviews, factory witness testing, and site startup.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;On-site generation engineering&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Own Initech&#39;s behind-the-meter generation architecture across the portfolio — prime-mover selection and sizing (reciprocating engines, gas turbines, fuel cells), paralleling topology, redundancy, fuel systems, and emissions controls — and maintain the generation basis of design and technical specifications that build partners and generation providers design against&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Set the day-one vs. day-N plant sizing and expansion strategy — what the plant needs on day one so it can be expanded or augmented later, and how to add units, storage, or a grid tie to a system already running&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Characterize the data center load for external generation partners — step changes, ramps, oscillation, fault behavior, and non-IT load — so providers can size and tune their plant against the real duty&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Model generation response against the load profile of large-scale ML training — step-load acceptance, block loading, transient frequency and voltage response, load rejection — and set the acceptance criteria (e.g., per ISO 8528-5) that generation packages are tested against&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Develop temporary- and bridging-generation strategies that deliver early site energization ahead of permanent utility service, including the sequencing, protection, and controls changes needed to transition from temporary to permanent power without stranding equipment or capacity&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Ensure generation designs meet NFPA 37, NFPA 110 where the plant provides emergency or legally required standby power, fuel-gas and fuel-storage codes (e.g., NFPA 54, NFPA 30), and applicable emissions requirements, and coordinate with environmental and permitting counterparts on the technical inputs to air permits&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Energy storage &amp;amp; microgrid architecture&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Size and specify battery energy storage systems for ride-through, step-load buffering, and power-quality support — including cell chemistry and enclosure selection, inverter selection (grid-forming vs. grid-following), UL 9540 listing, UL 9540A large-scale fire test data, and NFPA 855 installation requirements — and own the thermal and fire-protection interfaces&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Define the site microgrid topology and operating modes — grid-parallel, islanded, and black-start — and the transition logic between them, including load-shedding schemes, resynchronization criteria, and the conditions under which the site separates from and reconnects to the utility&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Specify the functional requirements for the microgrid controller — generation dispatch, set-point coordination across rotating and inverter-based sources, mode management — and drive its implementation, testing, and integration into site SCADA and the electrical power monitoring system (EPMS)&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Help define the protection and control requirements for generation and storage sources so that interconnection protection, anti-islanding, and source-transfer schemes are consistent from the generator terminals through the point of interconnection&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Grid interconnection &amp;amp; power quality&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Lead the technical side of utility interconnection for sites with on-site generation or storage — interconnection applications, studies, and agreements, ISO/RTO processes, IEEE 1547/2800 compliance, and interconnection protection&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Own power quality at the point of interconnection — flicker per IEEE 1453, harmonics per IEEE 519, voltage regulation, reactive-power and power-factor requirements — and design the generation, storage, and filtering mitigations needed to keep the site within its interconnection limits under real training-load behavior&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Run or critically review the power-system studies that support interconnection and microgrid design — load flow, short-circuit contribution from rotating and inverter-based sources, transient stability, motor-starting and step-load studies, and electromagnetic-transient studies where inverter controls matter&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Vendor diligence &amp;amp; delivery&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Lead technical due diligence on on-site generation providers, BESS integrators, and microgrid-controller vendors — evaluating equipment and controls on engineering merit, stress-testing performance and availability guarantees, and reviewing proposed architectures against Initech&#39;s basis of design&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Define the technical performance terms in energy-services agreements with on-site generation providers — availability, power quality, ramp, and ride-through, each with a definition, meter, test protocol, and acceptance criteria — working with energy commercial and legal counterparts&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Review and disposition design packages, submittals, shop drawings, and deviation requests from generation providers and their EPCs, and hold partners to Initech&#39;s reliability and maintainability requirements&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Support commissioning of generation, storage, and microgrid systems — witnessing factory and site acceptance tests, defining and observing integrated systems tests (islanding, resynchronization, black-start, load-step), and resolving field issues against design intent&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Manage concurrent generation and microgrid scopes across multiple sites, and contribute to the continuous improvement of Initech&#39;s generation and interconnection design standards as the portfolio and the technology both evolve&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have 10+ years of engineering experience in power generation, micr"}, "securityData": {"id": 5462966008, "title": "Security Data Engineer", "location": {"name": "Remote-Friendly (Travel Required) | San Francisco, CA"}, "content": "&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Initech&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Initech’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Gizmo is trained and served on hardware in data centers Initech operates and in sites partners build and run for us. DCSE secures that footprint: the sites, the hardware moving through them, and the people and vendors who touch it. Security at that scale runs on data, and you&#39;ll be the engineer who owns it and the systems that produce it: component-level hardware inventory and chain of custody, fed by software that runs at our sites and on hosts, and continuous control monitoring, with the posture calculations that decide what each site is cleared to run.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You set the architecture, agree schemas and interfaces with the teams, operators and vendors that own the sources, build the pipelines, stores and tools, and run what you ship. The goal is security that runs itself: custody, access and evidence verified continuously from records, with tools and AI agents doing the reviews. We favor simple, standard controls and tools that can be verified over elaborate ones. We use Gizmo throughout our engineering workflow and expect you to as well.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work with the rest of DCSE, including the engineers on its security monitoring platform, with Initech&#39;s compute and data center operations teams, and directly with data center operators, hardware vendors and logistics providers. The role is based in San Francisco, with remote applicants in the US considered, and involves regular travel to data center sites, which are critical infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware inventory and chain of custody:&lt;/strong&gt; own the component-level record of what hardware exists, where it is and who has handled it: the data model, the pipelines that join inventory and custody events from many source systems, change history on every record, and the tamper-evident stores behind it&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools, automation and AI agents:&lt;/strong&gt; build the tools and agents the team runs on this data: reconciliation, audit evidence exports, custody checks. When a review keeps costing people time, you build the tool or agent that retires it&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custody workflows and field software:&lt;/strong&gt; build the workflows and the site and host software that capture custody events as they happen (a receipt, a move, a data wipe, a decommission) and enforce who is authorized to record them&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous control monitoring and posture:&lt;/strong&gt; own the pipelines that turn check outcomes, assessment results and findings into per-control and per-site measures over time, against the compliance frameworks we and our partners are assessed against, and the posture calculation that decides what a site is cleared to run&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data quality:&lt;/strong&gt; build coverage checks, reconciliation against sources and alerts on a silent or drifting feed, so a wrong or missing record is caught the same day; own retention and access controls on the records&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration and reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; agree schemas and interfaces with the engineers who run the security monitoring platform, and build the query surfaces and reports the team, site leads and leadership use directly&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have designed and run production data systems (relational schemas, change data capture, batch or streaming pipelines and the services around them) and kept them correct: coverage measured, records reconciled against the source, alerts on silence, and a design that expects records to get corrupted or lost&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have integrated with systems you did not control (inventory tools, ticketing systems, vendor APIs) and built data models that outlive any one source&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have shipped software that runs outside a central service (host agents, site-local services, edge collectors) and kept it correct in the field, or built metrics a team made decisions on and defended them when challenged&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have worked hands-on with data about physical assets or security controls: a hardware fleet, data center or supply chain inventory, asset custody, or the control and evidence data of a security or compliance program&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Read and review other people&#39;s code, and build with AI coding agents using Git and code review&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Own a domain end to end: set the approach, design and build it with the teams and vendors whose systems it depends on, and run it as something people use every day&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Write SQL and at least one general-purpose programming language well&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Experience with asset management, supply chain or warehouse systems where serialized tracking and custody transfer are the core problem&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Experience building continuous control monitoring or metrics for a security or compliance program, or producing evidence an assessor accepted, for example against NIST SP 800-53, ISO 27001 or SOC 2&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Experience with risk or posture scoring that combines control results, findings and other evidence into a measure people make decisions on&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with data center hardware and its lifecycle from receipt to decommission, and with sites and parties you did not control: colocation, cloud or GPU cloud operators, hardware manufacturers, logistics providers&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have run software on many hosts or at remote sites with versioned rollout and a way to know each copy is still reporting&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Have built AI agents or automation that replaced recurring manual work&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$320,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$405,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For roles performing work in California: &lt;/strong&gt;We will consider for employment all qualified applicants, including those "}, "realData": {"id": 8396777, "title": "Data Engineer Tech Foundations", "location": {"name": "US - Remote"}, "content": "&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Hooli was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Engineer, Enterprise Core Datasets, Tech Foundations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;At Hooli, trustworthy data powers business decisions, product innovation, and operational efficiency. The Enterprise Core Datasets team builds the technical data foundations that help Hooli understand how the business operates, where resources are invested, and how new technologies create value.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Our scope spans high-impact datasets across the organization: measuring AI adoption, usage, and cost; understanding revenue, costs, and profitability through Unit Economics; integrating non-platform data from Jira and other enterprise applications; and powering critical company metrics such as Gross Booking Value and Revenue.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You will join a team that values thoughtful architecture, engineering rigor, and operational ownership. We collaborate with engineering, product, analytics, finance, and business teams to turn complex requirements into dependable, reusable data assets. We welcome engineers who are curious about the business and eager to learn and solve problems across diverse domains.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;As a Data Engineer, you will build and operate datasets that shape decisions across Hooli. Your work will help the organization measure AI adoption and spending, understand the economics of its products, and connect enterprise application data to meaningful business and operational insights.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You will deliver well-scoped data engineering projects, from requirements through design, implementation, validation, and production operations. You will work closely with teammates and stakeholders, with guidance from senior engineers on larger or more ambiguous problems. You will build maintainable data models and pipelines that accommodate new AI tools, products, cost categories, and enterprise systems while preserving clear definitions, traceability, and reliable historical data.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You will work in an ecosystem that includes petabyte-scale datasets, and you will help improve correctness, freshness, performance, and cost efficiency. You will contribute reusable components that simplify source onboarding and reduce duplicated logic. You will grow your craft through design reviews, code reviews, and mentorship from senior teammates.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Build, test, and operate data pipelines across AI usage and cost, Unit Economics, enterprise applications, and critical financial metrics.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Work with stakeholders and senior teammates to understand how AI adoption, consumption, and spending are measured, and implement data models that follow those definitions.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Extend Unit Economics datasets to connect revenue and diverse cost drivers.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Build ingestion and transformation pipelines for non-platform systems such as Jira and other BizTech enterprise applications.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Turn defined requirements into source contracts, reusable fact and dimension models, and technical designs for your projects, and get design feedback early.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Contribute to configurable pipelines and shared components that simplify onboarding new data sources and products.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Implement automated tests, reconciliation, and monitoring to protect data accuracy, completeness, and availability.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Support migrations and historical backfills by following dependency analysis, validation, and cutover plans.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Identify and fix performance and cost issues in distributed processing, storage, and queries.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Take part in the on-call rotation, respond to incidents, and improve runbooks for the datasets you own.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Participate in design and code reviews, share what you learn, and help improve Hooli&#39;s Data Engineering Paved Path.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;3+ years of relevant industry experience, with a Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering data engineering projects end to end, with increasing independence.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills and programming skills in Python or Scala, with experience writing maintainable, well-tested code.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with distributed processing such as Apache Spark, and familiarity with large-scale analytical storage systems.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Solid data modeling fundamentals, including fact and dimension design, slowly changing dimensions, incremental processing, and historical data management.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Experience working with varied data sources, such as APIs, enterprise applications, event data, and transactional systems, including handling schema changes.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Experience building reliable pipelines, and the ability to support migrations and backfills while preserving correctness and downstream compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of data quality checks, observability, lineage, and governance, and the ability to troubleshoot production data issues.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Ability to find and fix common performance bottlenecks in distributed computation, storage, and query execution.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and collaboration skills, including asking clarifying questions of business partners and explaining your technical choices.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Willingness to give and receive feedback in design and code reviews, and to help onboard teammates.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and sound judgment when learning new domains.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI usage or cost measurement, cloud cost attribution, Unit Economics, enterprise application data, or financial and payments datasets is a plus. Familiarity with workflow orchestration, SQL transformation frameworks, and modern table formats such as Apache Iceberg is also valuable.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Hooli office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a state where Hooli, Inc. has a registered entity. Click here for the up-to-date list of excluded states. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with us if the state you live in is on the exclusion list. If your position is employed by another Hooli entity, your recruiter will inform you what states you are eligible to work from.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Hooli is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We strive to also provide a disability inclusive application and interview process. If you are a candidate with a disability and require reasonable accommodation in order to submit an application, please contact us at: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;mailto:reasonableaccommodations@hooli.com&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;reasonableaccommodations@hooli.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. Please include your full name, the role you’re applying for and the accommodation necessary to assist you with the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;sp"}} });
})();
